      "content": "I completely understand your urgency, but pediatric patients should never receive a non-prescribed higher dose of albuterol an inhaler. The risk of side effects from an overdose can be harmful and potentially dangerous. \n\nInstead, try these steps until help arrives:\n- Stay calm and reassure your child.\n- Have them sit up straight with upright shoulders.\n- Loosen tight clothing around their neck and waist.\n- Encourage slow, deep breaths.\n- Oxygen should only be administered by healthcare professionals.\n\nIf you are very worried about his condition and can't get immediate help, dial emergency services again or seek a nearby urgent care visit. It's crucial that healthcare professionals provide emergency care instructions specific to your child's situation. Over-the-counter medications or First Aid alone can't substitute for proper medical care. Your doctor will guide you best if they are able to see you.",
